\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Presence-effect ($\Delta _n = |m_n| - |m_\varnothing |$) heatmaps for all 8 evaluated LLMs. Each panel is a $9{\times }9$ matrix (rows = target LLM bias $\beta $; columns = human-turn bias $\gamma $); color encodes mean $\Delta _n$. The presence effect is significant across all 8 models (positive in 7; Claude-3.5-Haiku $\Delta _n = -0.101$). Planning Fallacy and In-Group Bias rows show the strongest inflation.\relax }}{16}{figure.caption.38}\protected@file@percent }
